//! Corrections to rawler's camera colour matrices.
//!
//! rawler ships Adobe's XYZ->camera matrices for most cameras, but some
//! entries lack the Standard Light A calibration (so the matrix cannot follow
//! the white balance, see `color_calibration`) or carry a wrong D65 matrix:
//! the Sony ILCE-7M4 used the ILCE-7M3's, the Pentax K-S2's was scaled wrongly.
//! The values below are Adobe's ColorMatrix1 (A) and ColorMatrix2 (D65) as
//! written by Adobe DNG Converter, generated with
//! notes: scripts/reference/adobe_matrix_table.py. DNG files keep their own
//! matrices, except in-camera DNGs whose tags are unusable
//! (`replaces_dng_matrices`): Camera Raw renders those with its own profile.

